name wn-lmf
# A wordnet in WN-LMF (globalwordnet.github.io/schemas, WN-LMF-1.3.dtd). Read for each wordnet that is written in it
# (Open English WordNet, the Open Multilingual Wordnet's lexicons), each recipe naming its own witness.
#   A lexicon is its label. A lexical entry is its lemma's written form. A synset is the words it lists, in the order
#   listed (so every wordnet listing the same members lands on one entity); a sense is the word with its synset.
#   A syntactic behaviour is its frame, as written.
#   ids are the wordnet's keys: how it points at its things. Each resolves to the thing; members, synset, target and
#   senses are such keys. An ili is CILI's key of a concept, read as the concept; a lexfile is read as the lexicographer
#   file the highway lists.
#   What is no thing (a lemma, a relation, a definition) speaks of the nearest thing it is inside.
format xml

key LexicalEntry id
key Sense id
key Synset id
key SyntacticBehaviour id
thing Lexicon label
thing LexicalEntry Lemma/writtenForm
thing Sense synset within
thing Synset members
thing SyntacticBehaviour subcategorizationFrame
part members by space
part senses by space
# a member is written as the key of a lexical entry, or (as the Open Multilingual Wordnet writes it) of a sense, which
# stands for the entry it is inside
refer members LexicalEntry Sense within
refer synset Synset
refer SenseRelation.target Sense
refer SynsetRelation.target Synset
refer senses Sense
# a sense's subcat names the syntactic behaviours it takes, by their keys
part subcat by space
refer subcat SyntacticBehaviour
type ili ili
type lexfile lexfile
content label language writtenForm partOfSpeech relType subcategorizationFrame Definition ILIDefinition Example Pronunciation variety script Tag category Count ref lexicalized
# a file's bookkeeping, read by nothing: who made it, under what licence, at what version, how confident
# n (a sense's place among its entry's senses) and index (an entry's place among its homographs) number what the file
# already holds in order: the order is the path's, and the numbers are not read
omit n index
omit dc:* xmlns:* status note confidenceScore version url email license citation logo lexicographer adjposition

holds Lexicon Synset LexicalEntry SyntacticBehaviour
attest Lexicon language
attest Requires ref
holds LexicalEntry Sense
attest Lemma partOfSpeech script
attest Form writtenForm script
attest Pronunciation variety .
attest Tag category .
attest Sense synset subcat lexicalized
attest Count .
relate SenseRelation relType to target
# an ili written "in" is WN-LMF's mark for a concept proposed to CILI and not yet in it: it names no concept, and is said so
attest Synset ili partOfSpeech lexfile lexicalized Definition ILIDefinition Example
relate SynsetRelation relType to target
attest SyntacticBehaviour senses
